# .cursorrules - Developer Handoff Instructions

# 1. CORE TECH STACK CONSTRAINTS
- Frontend: React 19.2.8, Vite 6, React Router 7, Tailwind CSS v4
- Backend: Node.js v24.18.0 (ES Modules format), Express.js
- Database: MongoDB via Mongoose ODM
- Extension: removed — cloud-only product (Playwright workers on VPS)

# 2. DOCUMENTATION & HANDOFF STANDARDS
- Every single file must start with a comprehensive block comment outlining its architectural purpose, inputs, and down-stream system dependencies.
- Every function, custom hook, component, Express router, and Mongoose schema must feature complete inline JSDoc block documentation detailing parameter types, return values, and explicit business logic.
- Do not write abstract code; add comments explaining "Why" a specific approach was used, not just "What" the line does.

# 3. AUDIT TRAIL LOGGING
- For every prompt iteration, before changing any logic, append an entry to the top of `PROMPT_LOG.md` tracking the modification.

# 4. FORCE PROMPT DOCUMENTATION
- Always update `PROMPT_LOG.md` with: Prompt Provided, Architectural Flow, Impacted Files.

# 5. GIT PUSH + VPS DEPLOY POLICY
- After each completed prompt iteration, commit and push to `https://github.com/anumandlay/yambot.git` immediately (unless push credentials are unavailable — then report clearly).
- After every successful `git push`, always deploy to the VPS with:
  `python3 deploy/remote-deploy.py`
  Credentials come from untracked `deploy/.deploy.local.env` (see `.deploy.local.env.example`) or env `YAMBOT_SSH_*`. Never commit passwords.
- If deploy fails, report clearly; do not skip deploy silently.

# 6. ENVIRONMENT STRATEGY
- Maintain separate env files for local development and production.
- Production server should `git pull` without rewriting its secret `.env` values.
- Non-secret production base URLs live in committed `*.env.production` / Vite production env files.
- Secrets (Mongo URI, JWT secret, etc.) stay in server-local untracked `.env` / `.env.local` overlays.
- LLM credentials are stored per-user in MongoDB via the Settings page.

# 7. PRODUCT ARCHITECTURE
- Web app: auth, chats, goals/instructions, live results, Settings (LLM + DeathByCaptcha).
- Cloud worker: Playwright Chromium container per agent claims tasks via `/api/worker/*`.
- Mobile-first UI per `.cursor/rules/responsive.mdc`.
